	$$p(X,Y,Z)=p(X,Y)p(Y,Z)/p(Y)= p(X)p(Y|X)p(Z|Y),$$ the triplet $(X,Y,Z)$ is a Markov chain $X\rightarrow Y \rightarrow Z$~\citep[Equation 2.118]{cover91elements} and thus, by virtue of the data processing inequality~\citep[Theorem 2.8.1]{cover91elements}, the following inequality between mutual informations applies:
$$\label{eq:dpi}I(X;Y)\geq I(X;Z),\text{ namely } \quad h(X,Z)-h(X)+h(Z)\geq h(X,Y) -h(X)+h(Y)\geq -\alpha.$$

